  "_comment": "How detections map to the flat GTM fields. A detection belongs to a role when its name is in 'include' or one of its categories is in 'categories', and it is not in 'exclude'. 'prefer' orders single-value roles. 'evidence' limits a role to detections with evidence of those kinds (so Cloudflare DNS alone is not a CDN). Detections under 50% confidence are ignored. Platform, commerce, page-builder, framework, chat and booking roles need on-page evidence (or a CNAME for platforms): an SPF include (Zendesk, Intercom) says they send email with the tool, not that a widget is on the site.",
